# Frontend UI -> E2E Impact Rule

When changing UI-facing frontend code, always evaluate Playwright impact before finishing.

## Trigger scope

This applies to edits under `frontend/src/**` that affect:
- visible labels/text or accessibility names
- navigation flows, modal/dialog behavior, or form interactions
- element attributes used by tests (`data-testid`, role/name semantics)

## Required behavior

- Explicitly state one of:
  - `No E2E impact` with a short reason, or
  - `E2E updated` with touched files under `frontend/e2e/tests/**` and/or `frontend/e2e/pages/**`.
- If locators or test flows changed, run/update Playwright tests for the affected area.
- After Playwright test/page updates, append findings to `agents-results/locators-reviewer-results.md`.

## Do not

- Do not ship UI behavior changes with silent E2E drift.
- Do not rely on brittle selectors when stable test ids/role locators are available.
